  "reorder_method": "logit_compare.py --reorder's bounds for this model on this Mac: twice the worst, per measure, of the decode paths (step and verify, 192 rows each) of the two qmt_vs_qmr sources (a pure K-order change: the same half x half products, summed in fp32 in another order), median KL twice the worst median, the mean NLL change twice the worst of every path, the prefill rows included. Dumps: build/logit_dump flint-4bit (default windows) as the floor's, with NI_QMT=0 and/or NI_MATH_SAFE=1, on the build and Mac in \"measured\". The fast_vs_safe_math sources (the compiler's reassociation plus its precise functions: more than a reorder) are context, not in the gate. The gate bounds a reorder's drift only: near_tie (5.83) is the largest margin a pure reorder flipped, so a flip under it is not refused by itself; a change gated with it also shows the per-GEMM check against a double reference (bench_qmm / bench_moe) and the temperature-0 continuations of AGENTS.md, and the gate alone does not show that a change is a reorder. The bound is a 192-row draw (kept as it is: the orchestrator's call), and the 768-row qmt-vs-qmr check (rows_768) sits at its edge: step top-1 0.98047 against min_top1 0.979166 (a 17th flip in 768 fails it), and verify's tie margin 6.20 above near_tie 5.83 (its largest flip margin 2.59). A re-measure at 768 rows can therefore give a different reorder_gate, and a reorder near it can pass or fail on the draw.",
